 **L6  Each morning: the kept days of the daily games.** A rebuild of a bank (the cycle is read from today, so its blocks start today; CR-027) keeps today and the 7 days after it, the first 8 days of its first block, so a target that leaves its pool (a character hidden or marked spoiler, an idol switched off) stays the answer of its kept day, and `dle_guess` refuses its name: that day cannot be won, players can only give up. See it: `psql "$PROD_DB_URL" -X -At -f docs/launch/o1/checks/V-DLE-KEPT.sql` (VERIFY V-DLE): 0 on each game, counts only. Each such day also leaves one target of the pool out of that block (the gap between two days of a target still holds). If a row says KO: put the entry back as it was (its status or its review flag) until the last kept day; the next nightly refresh returns it to the pool and it can be removed again on the day after. If it must go at once, for a legal or safety reason, leave it out: that day's players can only give up. Never edit `dle_schedule` or `dle_entities` by hand.
